1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,474
Missing 40 years.

2
00:00:01,704 --> 00:00:02,924
Found turned to stone.

3
00:00:03,154 --> 00:00:05,105
That's what a newspaper said happened near

4
00:00:05,115 --> 00:00:07,045
Wanatah, in 1891.

5
00:00:07,595 --> 00:00:09,852
The story said a young woman vanished from

6
00:00:09,862 --> 00:00:11,957
her father's home, two miles south of

7
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:14,159
Wanatah, around 1851.

8
00:00:14,909 --> 00:00:17,334
Forty years later, it said, she was found

9
00:00:17,344 --> 00:00:19,207
in an abandoned bog-iron pit.

10
00:00:20,057 --> 00:00:21,955
The iron in the water had turned her to

11
00:00:21,965 --> 00:00:22,185
stone.

12
00:00:22,835 --> 00:00:23,869
But it was a hoax.

13
00:00:24,099 --> 00:00:25,745
There was no petrified woman.

14
00:00:26,195 --> 00:00:28,297
A local newsman named Harry Darling had

15
00:00:28,307 --> 00:00:29,490
made the whole thing up.

16
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:31,215
It still caused a stir.

17
00:00:31,445 --> 00:00:33,890
Wanatah's historical society tells of

18
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,564
people coming by train to see her, and

19
00:00:36,574 --> 00:00:38,292
being told there was no one to see.

20
00:00:38,942 --> 00:00:40,985
Comment your town, and it could be next.

